# derived - rebuild with `make`
build/

# dist/ is derived too, but the standalone is committed on purpose: it is the
# thing you actually hand someone, and the only other copy lives inside a CI
# zip. Re-run `make` and commit it again after anything that changes the model
# or the page, or the download goes stale. (Negation needs dist/* rather than
# dist/ - git will not look inside an excluded directory.)
dist/*
!dist/ombra-roma.html

# The cached OSM and elevation downloads ARE committed, on purpose: a cold fetch
# takes about an hour against public Overpass mirrors, and a failing mirror
# returns zero elements rather than an error. See CLAUDE.md.

node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Claude Code's local permission settings: machine-specific absolute paths,
# not project source.
.claude/
